WEBVTT

00:00:32.241 --> 00:00:36.370
Up next, daring daylight robbery
at a municipal swimming pool.

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:38.580
This is it. Turn me up.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.877
Earlier today, a foul-mouthed bandit
robbed the municipal pool

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:47.130
making off with the contents
of over three lockers.

00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:49.925
More like three lockers and a sink.

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:52.219
Bender, did you have
something to do with this?

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:53.428
Of course not.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:56.849
Holy spitz.
He's sporting skintight Speedos.

00:00:56.932 --> 00:00:58.851
They don't leave much to the imagination.

00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:01.186
Actually on a robot, they sorta do.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.397
One puny human got a look at the robber.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.399
Here we go. Here we go.

00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:08.318
Describing him as
a short, nasty, muscular...

00:01:08.402 --> 00:01:10.320
Yeah, make me famous, bighead.

00:01:10.404 --> 00:01:12.197
...Caucasian human male.

00:01:12.281 --> 00:01:13.532
What?

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:18.245
Hey! Now what am I supposed to watch
and drink all day?

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.163
This is an outrage.

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:22.791
What's the point of pulling
the biggest pool caper ever

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:24.126
if nobody knows you did it?

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:26.003
Well, there's the material rewards.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.504
You mean this junk?

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:30.048
Whee!

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:33.677
All I ever wanted was for people
to remember my name.

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:36.054
It's Bender.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.472
Oh, fuff!

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.516
Why bother remembering anything?

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.144
You're just going to forget it
five seconds later.

00:01:42.227 --> 00:01:43.854
It's so unfair.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:47.941
A debonair robot with
a zesty, in-your-face outlook

00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:52.154
doomed to obscurity like the rest of you,
especially Leela.

00:01:54.198 --> 00:01:57.534
If I died tomorrow,
no one would even notice.

00:02:02.581 --> 00:02:06.502
Boy, I've never seen him so down,
or ever before.

00:02:07.628 --> 00:02:10.130
How does a nobody like me get famous?

00:02:10.214 --> 00:02:11.840
I know.

00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:16.178
Hey, look. I'm stuck,
but I haven't given up hope.

00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:18.222
Call a soft-news journalist.

00:02:18.305 --> 00:02:19.640
You're not stuck.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.391
Shut up.

00:02:27.481 --> 00:02:29.608
Hey, everybody, do the "Bender."

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:31.485
This move's called the "Bender."

00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:37.324
Yo, Hot Wheels, this circle's about
free expression not fascist moves.

00:02:44.498 --> 00:02:47.334
A blank wall. Fame is mine.

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:09.815
There. Now no one will forget how I live
or my attitude regarding butt.

00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:15.529
All right, ladies. Let's flush
these artists' lofts straights to hell.

00:03:19.074 --> 00:03:22.160
No!

00:03:36.008 --> 00:03:39.094
I'm the first one to work. A new low.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.930
- Surprise!
- Happy funeral, Bender.

00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:46.101
A surprise funeral, for me?

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:49.021
We just wanted to show you
that you really will be remembered.

00:03:49.104 --> 00:03:52.482
Now, if the deceased will kindly
take his place of honor.

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:56.778
Ooh! Cushiony. And a minibar.

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:07.247
Dearly beloved, we are here today
to remember Bender,

00:04:07.539 --> 00:04:09.249
taken from us in the prime of life

00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:11.460
when he was crushed by a runaway semi

00:04:11.543 --> 00:04:13.170
driven by the Incredible Hulk.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:16.173
Aw! You knew my favorite cause of death.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:20.302
Now let us each remember the best things
about Bender, in our own way.

00:04:20.719 --> 00:04:21.929
Professor?

00:04:25.641 --> 00:04:30.187
Your standard bending unit
is made of an iron-osmium alloy.

00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:32.064
But Bender was different.

00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:35.651
Bender had a .04 percent nickel impurity.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.237
It's what made me me.

00:04:39.446 --> 00:04:42.366
If you ever needed a small package
brought into the country

00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:44.368
without a lot of X-raying and such,

00:04:44.493 --> 00:04:47.037
Bender always had a free body cavity.

00:04:47.621 --> 00:04:48.830
The professor's was better.

00:04:48.914 --> 00:04:51.250
Bender, shush. You're supposed to be dead.

00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:54.294
Say more about how great I am.
And where's the crying?

00:04:54.378 --> 00:04:56.463
You people look like
you're waiting for the bus.

00:04:59.883 --> 00:05:03.303
Oh, Danny boy, the pipes

00:05:03.387 --> 00:05:06.723
The pipes are calling

00:05:06.807 --> 00:05:07.850
Who-y boy?

00:05:07.933 --> 00:05:11.895
From glen to glen, and down...

00:05:11.979 --> 00:05:13.021
Danny boy?

00:05:13.105 --> 00:05:17.192
You're at my funeral, singing about
some dead stiff named Danny boy?

00:05:17.401 --> 00:05:19.653
You really are a massive bonehead.

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:21.238
I'm expressing my sorrow.

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:22.573
Get lost.

00:05:22.656 --> 00:05:25.993
I'd say, "Don't quit your day job,"
but you're awful at that, too.

00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:27.536
We're trying our best.

00:05:27.619 --> 00:05:29.162
Your best is an idiot.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.083
Let's pick it up, people.
So far, it's been crap after crap.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:35.460
I croaked. Now, show me some love.

00:05:38.213 --> 00:05:40.215
Bender was a truly special...

00:05:40.299 --> 00:05:43.051
Louder and sadder.

00:05:43.427 --> 00:05:45.637
Bender was a truly special...

00:05:45.721 --> 00:05:46.763
Next.

00:05:49.183 --> 00:05:51.560
- Dear Lord...
- Oh, next.

00:05:52.936 --> 00:05:55.689
Oh, Danny boy...

00:05:56.815 --> 00:06:00.611
Come on. Surely there must be someone here
who knows how great I was.

00:06:01.111 --> 00:06:02.487
Yes, there is, Bender.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.657
Bender was a lot of things
to a lot of people,

00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:09.703
but looking back, the number one thing
I can say about him is this,

00:06:10.078 --> 00:06:11.205
and simply this.

00:06:11.663 --> 00:06:13.582
Bender was my friend.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.668
What? That's it?

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.712
Who are you? You're nobody.

00:06:18.921 --> 00:06:20.589
This is the worst funeral ever.

00:06:22.925 --> 00:06:24.343
I hope you're all happy.

00:06:24.593 --> 00:06:27.513
You've succeeded in convincing me
life is worth living

00:06:27.638 --> 00:06:30.557
by showing how bad my funeral will suck.

00:06:33.602 --> 00:06:36.104
I know whose funeral
we'll be attending next.

00:06:36.647 --> 00:06:37.814
Oh, stop.

00:06:43.028 --> 00:06:44.488
News, everyone.

00:06:44.571 --> 00:06:49.618
Today you're going to O'Cyris IV
to deliver this enormous sandstone block.

00:06:50.452 --> 00:06:52.412
I thought something
looked different in here.

00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:10.138
Hi. We have a giant stone
to deliver. Sign here.

00:07:14.101 --> 00:07:18.021
Ah! Very nice. Much like
the ten million identical stones

00:07:18.105 --> 00:07:21.775
already used in the future tomb
of our great Pharaoh Hermenthotip.

00:07:22.609 --> 00:07:24.486
Impressive. Who's building it?

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:25.821
- You.
- Say again?

00:07:25.904 --> 00:07:28.740
You are now slaves of
the great Pharaoh Hermenthotip.

00:07:29.157 --> 00:07:30.158
Guards.

00:07:33.871 --> 00:07:37.624
Call it a hunch, but I've got
a bad feeling about this.

00:07:50.846 --> 00:07:53.056
You know, the worst thing
about being a slave,

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:55.475
they make you work
but they don't pay you or let you go.

00:07:55.684 --> 00:07:58.061
That's the only thing about being a slave.

00:07:58.145 --> 00:08:02.065
Attention. You are now possessions
of the great Pharaoh Hermenthotip,

00:08:02.316 --> 00:08:03.942
heir to the tenth dynasty,

00:08:04.109 --> 00:08:06.820
bringer of the good aspects
of the annual floods.

00:08:06.904 --> 00:08:10.240
Incredible. This place is just like
the ancient Egypt of my day.

00:08:10.324 --> 00:08:12.492
That is no coincidence.

00:08:12.576 --> 00:08:15.913
For our people visited your Egypt
thousands of years ago.

00:08:15.996 --> 00:08:19.917
- One.
- A billion.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.586
We learned many things
from the mighty Egyptians.

00:08:22.753 --> 00:08:25.088
Such as pyramid building, space travel,

00:08:25.255 --> 00:08:28.675
and how to prepare our dead
so as to scare Abbott and Costello.

00:08:32.054 --> 00:08:33.055
Also Wolfman.

00:08:34.932 --> 00:08:38.519
Look at these swanky tombs.
These people really know how to die.

00:08:38.602 --> 00:08:40.020
Are you crazy?

00:08:40.103 --> 00:08:43.398
They worked thousands of people to death
to make these stupid monuments.

00:08:43.482 --> 00:08:46.151
Hey, you spend your whole life
building a guy's toe,

00:08:46.235 --> 00:08:47.402
you're gonna remember him.

00:08:50.197 --> 00:08:52.699
I think I'm gonna like it here.

00:08:52.991 --> 00:08:55.035
Yeah, I noticed your sign
and I thought I'd come over...

00:08:58.121 --> 00:08:59.748
What we do is make you starve to death.

00:09:02.209 --> 00:09:04.545
One, two, three, pull.

00:09:05.003 --> 00:09:07.297
One, two, three, pull.

00:09:07.381 --> 00:09:09.466
Oh! Bloody chunder.

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:12.469
Pick it up, people.
We're enslaved here to do a job.

00:09:12.761 --> 00:09:15.055
Master, do we have to
count to three every time?

00:09:15.138 --> 00:09:17.891
Couldn't we count to one?
Or better yet, one-half?

00:09:17.975 --> 00:09:21.728
Good idea, slave. One-half, pull.
One-half, pull.

00:09:21.812 --> 00:09:23.188
Now we're slaving.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.744
Come on, guys.

00:09:37.828 --> 00:09:40.539
Pharaoh's counting on us.
Work faster. Like this.

00:09:46.837 --> 00:09:48.338
You call that motivating me?

00:09:48.422 --> 00:09:49.715
Don't just whip with your arms.

00:09:49.798 --> 00:09:52.050
The power comes from your hips. Like this.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:58.140
Bender, quit giving
the slave drivers pointers.

00:09:58.223 --> 00:10:00.100
Yeah. Remember who your real friends are.

00:10:00.184 --> 00:10:02.269
I'll tell you who I remember.

00:10:02.811 --> 00:10:06.607
Enupsis. Pleotut. What's-his-name.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:09.818
He was the greatest of all.

00:10:12.738 --> 00:10:15.032
Pharaoh Hermenthotip approaches.

00:10:28.587 --> 00:10:32.466
Hurry, hurry. Pharaoh's coming.
Get that nose in place. Come on.

00:10:52.528 --> 00:10:56.448
Excellent work.
I'm very proud of all you slaves.

00:10:58.033 --> 00:11:00.327
Whoo hoo! Viva Hermenthotip.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:03.163
And now, I have a grand announcement.

00:11:03.247 --> 00:11:06.458
In honor of your achievement,
you're all hereby...

00:11:08.877 --> 00:11:10.420
No!

00:11:16.593 --> 00:11:18.846
Tell the slaves they can all go...

00:11:18.929 --> 00:11:21.890
Go faster? I told them,
but they're so damn lazy.

00:11:21.974 --> 00:11:25.018
No. I mean, they're all free.

00:11:25.102 --> 00:11:27.020
Freeloading off you? I agree.

00:11:27.104 --> 00:11:28.647
No, I...

00:11:34.444 --> 00:11:36.655
Pharaoh Hermenthotip is dead.

00:11:37.948 --> 00:11:39.867
He's whipping angels now.

00:11:49.793 --> 00:11:52.337
We commend the body
of the great Hermenthotip

00:11:52.588 --> 00:11:54.506
to the abode of the damned.

00:11:54.965 --> 00:11:56.258
The damned good-looking.

00:11:57.342 --> 00:11:59.511
Pharaoh commanded me
to tell that joke at his funeral.

00:12:03.807 --> 00:12:07.227
I'll always remember you, Hermenthotip.

00:12:07.311 --> 00:12:11.857
To equip Pharaoh for his journey,
we bury him with his favorite possessions.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.150
Such as his heart and liver.

00:12:16.361 --> 00:12:19.531
And the many goods he left
in his royal garage.

00:12:23.577 --> 00:12:27.247
Also this bag of cats
our culture considers holy.

00:12:32.211 --> 00:12:37.508
Pharaoh, my god king,
You are cold and deceased

00:12:37.591 --> 00:12:40.344
I used to have him sing

00:12:41.512 --> 00:12:43.805
P-P-P-Pharaoh and his pets

00:12:47.351 --> 00:12:50.687
But the years went by
And Pharaoh died

00:12:50.771 --> 00:12:53.774
Susie will have joined him
In the afterlife

00:12:56.109 --> 00:12:57.819
Hermenthotip is gone.

00:12:57.903 --> 00:13:00.405
The time to designate a new Pharaoh
is at hand.

00:13:03.408 --> 00:13:04.409
Wow.

00:13:04.493 --> 00:13:07.913
At dawn tomorrow, the high priest
will consult the Wall of Prophecy

00:13:07.996 --> 00:13:10.332
to determine Hermenthotip's successor.

00:13:12.543 --> 00:13:13.544
Whoo!

00:13:13.627 --> 00:13:15.504
That concludes the funeral.

00:13:15.754 --> 00:13:18.757
You don't have to go home,
but you can't stay here.

00:13:21.969 --> 00:13:24.388
Can you believe it? Pharaoh's dead.

00:13:24.471 --> 00:13:28.600
Yes. Tonight we are slaves to no one.
Except the rhythm.

00:13:29.935 --> 00:13:32.437
Yeah. Play those bongos.

00:13:32.521 --> 00:13:34.690
I'm gonna spin till I fall down.

00:13:34.773 --> 00:13:36.567
Whoo!

00:13:53.584 --> 00:13:57.462
We interrupt this ancient prophecy
to bring you a late-breaking bulletin.

00:14:05.137 --> 00:14:07.097
Great Wall of Prophecy.

00:14:07.181 --> 00:14:10.934
Reveal to us
God's will that we may blindly obey.

00:14:11.143 --> 00:14:14.062
Free us from thought and responsibility.

00:14:14.146 --> 00:14:16.315
We shall read things off you.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:17.900
Then do them.

00:14:17.983 --> 00:14:19.735
Your words guide us.

00:14:19.818 --> 00:14:20.861
We're dumb.

00:14:20.944 --> 00:14:23.739
You know what else stinks
about being a slave? The hours.

00:14:25.407 --> 00:14:29.453
The prophecy is strange
and crudely drawn at best.

00:14:29.536 --> 00:14:32.039
It indicates that we are here...

00:14:33.207 --> 00:14:37.711
...and our next Pharaoh
is over there, near some tents.

00:14:37.794 --> 00:14:41.798
Those are waves, jackass.
It's supposed to be a river.

00:14:43.217 --> 00:14:45.469
Hey, I think I know
who the next Pharaoh is.

00:14:45.552 --> 00:14:46.553
Oh, Lord.

00:14:46.637 --> 00:14:51.558
We hear your voice, great Pharaoh.
Reveal yourself to us.

00:14:52.351 --> 00:14:57.147
Behold. I have emerged
from the place of spells and fairies.

00:14:58.732 --> 00:15:02.945
It is he, just as
the Wall of Prophecy prophesied.

00:15:05.197 --> 00:15:07.616
Long live Pharaoh Bender.

00:15:07.699 --> 00:15:10.077
Long live Pharaoh Bender.

00:15:10.577 --> 00:15:12.704
This society is a bunch of idiots.

00:15:16.917 --> 00:15:18.460
People of O'Cyris IV.

00:15:18.544 --> 00:15:21.588
Please welcome a man
who started as a slave,

00:15:21.672 --> 00:15:24.925
but worked his way up
to lord of all creation.

00:15:25.008 --> 00:15:27.845
Our new Pharaoh, Bender.

00:15:37.646 --> 00:15:43.068
Citizens of me. The cruelty of
the old Pharaoh is a thing of the past.

00:15:45.153 --> 00:15:50.200
Let a whole new wave of cruelty
wash over this lazy land.

00:15:51.869 --> 00:15:53.161
- Huh?
- What? What did he say?

00:15:53.245 --> 00:15:55.497
Hear the word of Pharaoh.

00:15:55.581 --> 00:15:58.709
Build unto me a statue
of ridiculous proportion.

00:15:58.792 --> 00:16:01.295
One billion cubits in height

00:16:01.378 --> 00:16:05.465
that I might be remembered
for all eternity.

00:16:05.716 --> 00:16:07.009
And be quick about it.

00:16:14.766 --> 00:16:17.102
Lowly slave. Why are you not working?

00:16:17.186 --> 00:16:18.478
I am.

00:16:18.562 --> 00:16:20.397
I meant, "Yourself to death?"

00:16:21.398 --> 00:16:23.567
Mighty Pharaoh, it hurts when I breathe.

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:26.486
Well, then, what do you think
you should stop doing?

00:16:27.487 --> 00:16:28.739
Crawl, pigs.

00:16:28.822 --> 00:16:30.199
Ow!

00:16:30.282 --> 00:16:33.076
The Pharaoh has spoken.

00:17:02.022 --> 00:17:06.360
Your task is nearly completed.
Don't let down Pharaoh now.

00:17:14.284 --> 00:17:16.787
The great monument
is finished, oh, Pharaoh.

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:18.997
And now the unveiling.

00:17:20.791 --> 00:17:21.834
Hmm.

00:17:22.376 --> 00:17:24.461
Remember me.

00:17:25.254 --> 00:17:27.256
Remember me.

00:17:28.298 --> 00:17:30.133
Remember me.

00:17:30.217 --> 00:17:31.927
Does it please you, my lord?

00:17:32.219 --> 00:17:33.470
Mmm.

00:17:33.554 --> 00:17:34.930
It's a good start.

00:17:36.974 --> 00:17:38.892
Yeah, it's definitely big, all right.

00:17:39.142 --> 00:17:41.854
I just wonder if it's too big, you know?

00:17:41.937 --> 00:17:45.607
I mean, are people gonna be
remembering me or the statue?

00:17:45.691 --> 00:17:48.735
But, sire, we made it
to your exact specifications.

00:17:48.819 --> 00:17:50.737
Too exact, if you ask me.

00:17:50.946 --> 00:17:52.447
Tear it down and try again.

00:17:52.573 --> 00:17:55.075
But this time, don't embarrass yourselves.

00:17:58.704 --> 00:17:59.955
Yeah. That's right.

00:18:00.789 --> 00:18:01.915
What...

00:18:03.458 --> 00:18:06.503
Ladies and gentlemen,
the Pharaoh suddenly died.

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:08.380
Yay!

00:18:11.341 --> 00:18:12.342
Good riddance.

00:18:12.426 --> 00:18:16.388
What about my servants?

00:18:16.471 --> 00:18:17.639
- Yeah.
- Right.

00:18:28.901 --> 00:18:31.528
Bender, I really hope that's you,
because if it isn't...

00:18:33.989 --> 00:18:34.990
we're in trouble.

00:18:35.073 --> 00:18:38.160
You jerk. Why'd you have to drag us along?

00:18:38.243 --> 00:18:40.037
I wanted to watch you remember me.

00:18:44.041 --> 00:18:47.628
Did you really think you'd need
all this junk in the afterlife?

00:18:47.711 --> 00:18:48.754
Afterlife?

00:18:49.213 --> 00:18:51.465
If I thought I had to go through
a whole another life,

00:18:51.548 --> 00:18:52.925
I'd kill myself right now.

00:18:53.008 --> 00:18:56.053
Well, rot in peace. Fry and I are leaving.

00:18:56.136 --> 00:18:58.055
Sorry, but we're totally sealed in.

00:18:58.639 --> 00:19:02.100
Nothing can get in or out
except millions of snakes.

00:19:03.477 --> 00:19:06.605
Here, have a pomegranate schnapps
from my private distillery

00:19:06.688 --> 00:19:09.274
and start sharing
fond memories of me, Bender.

00:19:10.859 --> 00:19:12.986
What proof is this? Some huge number?

00:19:15.948 --> 00:19:16.990
It's explosive.

00:19:17.074 --> 00:19:19.701
Maybe we could escape
by setting fire to the distillery

00:19:19.785 --> 00:19:21.578
and blowing this place to rubble.

00:19:24.414 --> 00:19:26.166
Let's get a little kindling going.

00:19:30.212 --> 00:19:33.590
No! You can't blow up my monument.
I won't be remembered.

00:19:33.674 --> 00:19:36.802
Oh, right. How selfish of me.

00:19:36.885 --> 00:19:38.387
We'll just stay here forever.

00:19:38.846 --> 00:19:42.057
Hey, Fry, remember that robot, Bender?

00:19:42.933 --> 00:19:45.269
Bend-er? Doesn't ring a bell.

00:19:46.478 --> 00:19:47.813
Did you hear something, Leela?

00:19:47.896 --> 00:19:51.275
No, but I bet it wasn't someone
who was good at stealing.

00:19:51.358 --> 00:19:54.778
Stop it. Stop it. It's not right.
You've crossed a line!

00:19:54.862 --> 00:19:56.613
Hey, Leela, you know who I remember?

00:19:56.697 --> 00:19:57.823
Oh, please let it be me.

00:19:57.906 --> 00:20:00.284
That guy who used to bend things,
you know?

00:20:00.367 --> 00:20:01.952
- Me? Please?
- Hermes.

00:20:02.035 --> 00:20:03.745
All right, all right.

00:20:04.538 --> 00:20:08.250
If it means that much to you,
blow up my statue.

00:20:08.375 --> 00:20:12.171
Oh, Bender.
When did you come in? Hold still.

00:20:22.097 --> 00:20:23.599
Let's blow this tomb.

00:20:34.735 --> 00:20:38.447
Pharaoh Bender.
He once more walks among the living.

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:39.573
How we doing?

00:20:52.211 --> 00:20:54.171
Remember me.

00:20:55.464 --> 00:20:57.841
I will. I will.

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:11.063
Please just leave me alone.

00:21:15.192 --> 00:21:18.487
Bender, I understand your desire
to be remembered,

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:20.364
but you don't need a statue for that.

00:21:21.365 --> 00:21:22.366
I don't?

00:21:22.449 --> 00:21:23.700
No.

00:21:23.784 --> 00:21:27.037
You have your legacy as a brutal,
tyrannical dictator,

00:21:27.162 --> 00:21:29.331
and that will outlive any monument.

00:21:30.541 --> 00:21:31.959
You really think they'll remember me?

00:21:32.042 --> 00:21:33.460
Absolutely.

00:21:33.836 --> 00:21:37.339
Well, in that case, one planet down.

00:21:37.756 --> 00:21:41.718
Helmsmen, set course for Earth.

00:21:47.182 --> 00:21:48.392
That's not Earth.

00:21:48.475 --> 00:21:49.852
Oh.